    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "090de165_97a875a0",
        "filename": "core/minute-ia/panic.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 202,
      "author": {
        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-07T17:38:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue is here: https://crrev.com/f9a512fb73ad1ac4b69673770eeddb2dac6712c9/common/system.c#828\n\nPanic data persists just like reset flags in ISH, and the panic data will contain important info, such as the EIP when WDT IRQ happened.\n\nWe can probably get around this by setting the vector to PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG when the vector passed in is ISH_WDT_VEC in exception_panic, and that way the if statement in common/system.c will be false, and initializing the structure here should be OK.",
      "parentUuid": "b3ac72ed_bfacf39a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 202,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "98a3623c7dca05b93e1ef84f2674211e3e2e29f9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
